-- `a && b` over two draw-bound coins, as an element of a list. It used to be
-- refused (set-valued witness construction failed for 'a'): the draws could
-- not sink past the list's literal tail into the operands of `&&`. They do
-- since task compositional-answers-enumerate-heard-jointly. The helper over a
-- draw-bound record compiles too since the same task (enumerability/andInsideHelperOverRecordDraw).
-- Task and-inside-list-or-helper-over-draws-refused.
main = draw a = Uniform < 0.3 in draw b = Uniform < 0.6 in [a && b]
